type: software
title: "Le Bureau de Hương: an offline 3D office with a mode-of-entry board for International Business teaching"
abstract: >-
  A small 3D office that runs entirely in the browser and makes no network
  request at all. Visitors walk in, meet six characters, and read what the
  author's dissertation studies. Every answer is written in advance by the
  author and stored in the page; nothing is generated at run time. Je
  m'appelle Hương is the author herself; the other five characters are
  fictional. An Entry Mode Simulator re-scores six entry modes for the
  Japanese market with five priority sliders, using illustrative figures from
  BizOn AIBIS with the co-author's consent. A mode-of-entry board orders seven
  modes by rising resource commitment, each anchored to a standard
  International Business theory (Uppsala model, transaction-cost economics,
  agency theory, CAGE framework, resource-based view, born-global
  perspective, Dunning's OLI paradigm). Bilingual Vietnamese-English, with no
  server, no build step, no analytics and no third-party request. Used as
  open teaching material for an undergraduate International Business course.
  Formerly titled Research Office.
